  "body": "Add 4th-axis `.mch` machine variants for Brother Speedio S500X2 and S700X2 with the Brother T-200A rotary table, and add safe 3+1 rotary indexing in `brother-speedio.cps`.\n\n## Scope\n- Add `assets/machines/brother-s500x2-t200a.mch` and `assets/machines/brother-s700x2-t200a.mch` modeling an `A` rotary axis about `X` (`axis_to_table: 170.0` mm, max `36,000.0` deg/min = `100` rpm, `rtcp: false`), following `assets/machines/tormach-770mx-microarc4.mch` and `assets/machines/doosan-dnm.mch`.\n- Register both `.mch` files in `MACHINES` (`crates/app/src/posting.rs`) and `crates/app/tests/machine.rs`.\n- Update `assets/posts/brother-speedio.cps` to post 3+1 indexed `A` positions safely on non-RTCP rotary machines, emit an explicit initial `A` word (`A0` included) after every tool change (`doosan-dnm.cps` rule), and refuse continuous RTCP tilt when `rtcp` is false.\n- Output configurable rotary clamp and unclamp M-codes on separate blocks around `A` moves so shop-specific ladder codes (`M10`/`M11` or `M440`–`M445`) match the machine.\n- Guard `G100` blocks so no `A` word appears on 3-axis machines where no rotary axis exists.\n\nDone means: both `T-200A` `.mch` files validate in `crates/app/tests/machine.rs`, `brother-speedio.cps` passes rotary indexing tests including explicit `A0` reset and clamping order in `crates/post/tests/brother_speedio_post.rs`, and 3-axis `G100` blocks refuse or omit unconfigured `A` moves.\n\nPart of #1960\n",
